# Roles

Two roles: `owner` and `staff`. Defined in `@/lib/permissions.ts`.
- `owner` — full access to everything including billing, plans, and event management
- `staff` — can manage members/visits/own profile; read-only on org, event types/categories; no billing

# Checking Permissions

```ts
// In components (client):
const { usePermissions } = useUser();     // exposes can(), role, etc.

// In server/API:
import { can, isOwner } from "@/lib/permissions";
can("staff", "members", "delete")  // false
can("owner", "members", "delete")  // true
```

# Trial Enforcement — Four Layers

Always apply all relevant layers when adding new protected functionality:

| Layer | File | What it does |
|-------|------|-------------|
| Middleware | `src/lib/supabase/middleware.ts` | Redirects expired trial users from page routes before render |
| Server page guard | `src/lib/trial-server.ts` → `requireTrialAccess()` | Called at top of each server page; redirects before any data fetch |
| API layer | `src/lib/api-permissions.ts` → `requirePermission()` | Returns 402 for blocked resources when trial expired |
| Client SWR guard | `src/hooks/useTrialGuard.ts` → `useTrialGuard(error)` | Redirects to billing if SWR error has `.status === 402` |

# Trial-Allowed Resources (always accessible)

`billing`, `plans`, `profile`, `organization` — defined in `TRIAL_ALLOWED_RESOURCES` in `@/lib/trial.ts`.

# When Adding a New Protected Page

1. Add path to `protectedRoutes` in middleware if not already covered by a prefix
2. Call `requireTrialAccess(profile.organizationId)` in the server page component
3. Use `requirePermission(resource, action)` in the API route handler
4. Call `useTrialGuard(error)` in the SWR client container
